{"dossier":"D06","entry_points":[{"sids":["mm/memory.c::page_ptl_cachep","mm/memory.c::ptlock_cache_init","mm/memory.c::ptlock_alloc","mm/memory.c::ptlock_free"],"text":"Slab cache holds locks; init panics on failure, alloc attaches, free releases."},{"sids":["mm/mempolicy.c::change_prot_numa","mm/mprotect.c::change_protection","mm/mprotect.c::change_protection_range","mm/mprotect.c::change_p4d_range","mm/mprotect.c::change_pud_range","mm/mprotect.c::change_pmd_range","mm/mprotect.c::change_prepare","mm/mprotect.c::pgtable_split_needed"],"text":"NUMA applies over intervals gathering and counting. Change rejects bad combos, huge uses dedicated path. Walk populates missing, skips absent, splits partial huge, batches with lazy invalidation. Controls select NUMA and userfault set, clear and resolve; split for marker tracking."},{"sids":["mm/mempolicy.c::do_migrate_pages.alt_1","mm/mempolicy.c::do_migrate_pages.alt_2","mm/mempolicy.c::migrate_to_node","mm/mempolicy.c::alloc_migration_target_by_mpol.alt_1","mm/mempolicy.c::alloc_migration_target_by_mpol.alt_2"],"text":"Queue selects lock, walks, faults if untouched else failures. Single isolates with gap tolerance then migrates. Global loops pairs without LRU. Targets adjust by order, or unimplemented by build."}],"exports":[{"sids":["mm/memory.c::remap_pfn_range","mm/memory.c::remap_pfn_range_prepare_vma","mm/memory.c::remap_pfn_range_complete","mm/memory.c::do_remap_pfn_range.alt_2","mm/memory.c::__simple_ioremap_prep","mm/memory.c::simple_ioremap_prepare","mm/memory.c::vm_iomap_memory"],"text":"Remap aligns end, resolves copy-on-write, derives offset and masks flags, then delegates; completion uses pending action. IO validates range, converts to frame and installs."},{"sids":["mm/memory.c::apply_to_page_range","mm/memory.c::apply_to_existing_page_range","mm/memory.c::__apply_to_page_range","mm/memory.c::apply_to_p4d_range","mm/memory.c::apply_to_pud_range","mm/memory.c::apply_to_pmd_range","mm/memory.c::apply_to_pte_range","mm/pgtable-generic.c::pgd_clear_bad","mm/pgtable-generic.c::p4d_clear_bad","mm/pgtable-generic.c::pud_clear_bad"],"text":"Range walk callbacks per entry, creating or visiting-only; rejects bad ranges and huge leaves, clears malformed when creating, syncs kernel maps, holds entry locks with deferred flush."},{"sids":["mm/mempolicy.c::__mpol_put","mm/mempolicy.c::vma_migratable","mm/mempolicy.c::mempolicy_set_node_perf"],"text":"Policy release uses RCU-deferred reclaim. Migratable excludes device, DAX, huge and low-zone file. Node perf updates bandwidth, recomputes auto weights leaving manual frozen, publishes under lock."}],"extracts":["8544554341569266ba2b066dfa3c35dcd546ab54fa080acdbfea7952884b0cbd","c1324d09311cb553a33f1e4764940973fde3b513ec2ba5a537618ee635c0fa96","ca964e969b3d03c5cf2d370ce4731e1fa4ac30f72a9a12f830d37ac7bb79246f"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["mm/mprotect.c::change_protection","mm/mprotect.c::change_protection_range"],"text":"Bad userfault warns once and no-ops instead of mixed update. Empty or reversed protection range violates precondition and triggers bug check."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["mm/mmap.c::expand_stack","mm/mmap.c::vma_expand_up.alt_1","mm/mmap.c::vma_expand_down.alt_1","mm/mmap.c::vma_expand_up.alt_2","mm/mmap.c::vma_expand_down.alt_2","mm/nommu.c::expand_stack"],"text":"Growth drops read for killable write lock, re-resolves area, succeeds if inside, tries up then down, downgrades on success. Direction support is build-dependent; without VM, growth always fails."},{"sids":["mm/mempolicy.c::numa_nearest_node","mm/mempolicy.c::nearest_node_nodemask","mm/mempolicy.c::reduce_interleave_weights"],"text":"Nearest picks smallest distance, returning input if satisfying or no-node. Weights scale with bandwidth share floored at one, normalized by GCD. Node ids use state, sentinel and bounds."},{"sids":["mm/mempolicy.c::mpol_rebind_task","mm/mempolicy.c::mpol_rebind_mm","mm/mempolicy.c::mpol_new_nodemask","mm/mempolicy.c::mpol_new_preferred","mm/mempolicy.c::mpol_rebind_policy","mm/mempolicy.c::mpol_rebind_nodemask"],"text":"Task and address rebind adjust to new allowance under write lock. Creation rejects empty, preferred keeps first. Rebind skips absent, local and equal, else per-mode with static, relative or remap."},{"sids":["mm/mempolicy.c::strictly_unmovable","mm/mempolicy.c::queue_folios_pte_range","mm/mempolicy.c::queue_folios_hugetlb","mm/mempolicy.c::queue_folio_required","mm/mempolicy.c::queue_folios_pmd","mm/mempolicy.c::migrate_folio_add.alt_1"],"text":"Strict without move fails fast. Match mask with invert, skip bad. Dedup large. Avoid shared unless all, isolate; huge counts migration failures."},{"sids":["mm/vma.c::vma_modify_policy","mm/mempolicy.c::queue_pages_walk_ops","mm/mempolicy.c::queue_pages_lock_vma_walk_ops","mm/mempolicy.c::queue_pages_range","mm/mempolicy.c::vma_replace_policy","mm/mempolicy.c::queue_pages_test_walk","mm/mempolicy.c::mbind_range"],"text":"Queue carries list, mask, bounds, first and failures; ops differ in read versus write lock. Validation rejects gaps unless allowed, skips non-migratable. Bind clamps, returns if equal else splits and replaces."},{"sids":["mm/mempolicy.c::do_set_mempolicy","mm/mempolicy.c::do_get_mempolicy","mm/mempolicy.c::get_policy_nodemask","mm/mempolicy.c::lookup_node"],"text":"Set validates under task lock, publishes, resets cursor. Query rejects unknown, handles allowed, faults on miss, resolves by page or cursor, masks internal, prefers user."}],"locks":[{"sids":["mm/mprotect.c::change_pte_range","mm/mprotect.c::mprotect_folio_pte_batch","mm/mprotect.c::change_pmd_prepare"],"text":"Maps table under spinlock with retry, drains batches, uses lazy MMU. Filtering skips conforming, checks NUMA, probes unflagged and flagged; empty installs markers for userfault file."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F1"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F3"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["mm/memory.c::pfnmap_args_setup","mm/memory.c::pfnmap_lockdep_assert","mm/memory.c::follow_pfnmap_start","mm/memory.c::follow_pfnmap_end","mm/memory.c::generic_access_phys"],"text":"Lookup under address lock checks flags, descends lockless, locks huge with retry, maps entries, returning held lock and frame from base plus offset. Phys snapshots, checks write, maps, revalidates, copies."},{"sids":["mm/memory.c::__access_remote_vm","mm/memory.c::access_remote_vm","mm/memory.c::access_process_vm","mm/memory.c::__copy_remote_vm_str","mm/memory.c::copy_remote_vm_str","mm/memory.c::__might_fault"],"text":"Remote locks, untags, ensures area, pins and copies with dirty, using hooks. String NUL pagewise to bound. Might checks when enabled."},{"sids":["mm/mprotect.c::change_present_ptes","mm/mprotect.c::prot_commit_flush_ptes","mm/mprotect.c::change_softleaf_pte","mm/mprotect.c::set_write_prot_commit_flush_ptes","mm/mprotect.c::commit_anon_folio_batch","mm/mprotect.c::page_anon_exclusive_batch"],"text":"Present updates protection and markers, restores none when trapping, promotes or commits with flush. Soft reads migration and device, keeps poison and guard, clears on resolve. Shared whole, private by exclusive."}],"structs":[{"sids":["mm/memory.c::__read_mostly.alt_3","mm/memory.c::fault_around_bytes_get","mm/memory.c::fault_around_bytes_set","mm/memory.c::fault_around_debugfs","mm/mempolicy.c::MPOL_MF_DISCONTIG_OK","mm/mempolicy.c::MPOL_MF_INVERT","mm/mempolicy.c::MPOL_MF_WRLOCK","mm/mempolicy.c::weightiness"],"text":"Fault-around count has byte view shifted; default 65536 [CITED] scaled, rejects oversize, clamps and rounds to power of two. Weightiness 32 [CITED], flags shift 0 [CITED],1 [CITED],2 [CITED]. Debug mode 0644 [CITED]."},{"sids":["mm/mempolicy.c::policy_cache","mm/mempolicy.c::sn_cache","mm/mempolicy.c::default_policy","mm/mempolicy.c::preferred_node_policy","mm/mempolicy.c::weighted_interleave_state","mm/mempolicy.c::wi_state","mm/mempolicy.c::node_bw_table","mm/mempolicy.c::wi_state_lock","mm/mempolicy.c::mpol_ops.alt_2","mm/mempolicy.c::mempolicy_operations","mm/mempolicy.c::mpol_ops.alt_1","mm/mempolicy.c::migration_mpol","mm/mempolicy.c::queue_pages"],"text":"Caches policies and nodes, local default, per-node preferred, weighted state with weights guarded by mutex, bandwidth table. Ops pair create and rebind across default, interleave, preferred, bind, local, preferred-many and weighted modes. Contexts carry policy, position, list, mask and counts."}],"stubs":[{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_3","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/cacheflush.h::copy_from_user_page","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/err.h::IS_ERR","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/page-flags.h::page_folio","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock.h::spin_unlock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock_rt.h::spin_unlock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/uaccess.h::untagged_addr_remote","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D01"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::BUG_ON.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::BUG_ON.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON.alt_3","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/cacheflush.h::copy_to_user_page","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/debug